Giant Apple Cinnamon Roll Cake
  --Rosana Machiela

Dough:
4 c (500 g) ap flour
1/4 c (55 g) light brown sugar
1/3 c (66 g) sugar
1/2 tsp baking powder
1/2 tsp kosher salt
1 packet instant yeast*
8 tbsp (113.4 g) unsalted butter, melted
1 c (8 oz) whole milk
1 large egg, room temperature

In a large bowl, whisk together the all purpose flour, light brown sugar, granulated sugar, baking powder, salt and instant yeast. Transfer to the stand mixer bowl. In a small saucepan or microwave safe bowl, melt the butter. Cool slightly and add the milk, whisking to avoid clumps. Heat to 110F and transfer to a bowl. Whisk in the eggs. Using the hook attachment, pour the wet ingredients into the dry mixture. Mix on low for 5 min, increase speed to medium-high for another 5 min, until dough comes together. It should be tacky but not too sticky. Transfer to a floured surface and knead for 3-4 min. Form into a bowl and transfer to a greased bowl. Cover with a towel, and allow to rise in a warm place for 1 hr. Dough will double in size. Lightly flour a surface and roll out the dough to a 12x15" rectangle. 

Filling:
8 tbsp (113.4 g) unsalted butter, softened
2 tbsp ground cinnamon
1/4 tsp nutmeg, grated or ground
3/4 c (150 g) light brown sugar
1 1/2 c (120 g) apple, finely diced (~1 1/4 apples)

In a large bowl, using a silicone spatula, combine the softened butter, cinnamon, nutmeg and brown sugar. Spread the cinnamon filling all over the dough. Sprinkle the finely diced apples on top. Using a dough or pizza cutter, cut the dough lengthwise, 3 times, into 4 even strips. Starting from the bottom, roll the first strip to the top. Place the end of first roll on top of the second strip, and roll again from bottom to top. Repeat with the remaining strips of dough until you have a giant roll. Place on 11" skillet lined with parchment paper. Cover with plastic wrap or a kitchen towel for 30 min. Preheat oven to 350F. Bake apple cinnamon roll cake for 30 min. Cover with foil and reduce oven temperature to 325F. Bake for an additional 25-30 minutes, until light golden and set in the middle. Let the roll cool 10 min before icing.

Icing:
8 oz full fat cream cheese, softened
1/4 c (2 oz) whole milk
3 c (325 g) powdered sugar, sifted
1 tsp vanilla extract
2 tsp maple syrup
Pinch of kosher salt

In the bowl of a stand mixer fitted with the paddle attachment, beat the softened cream cheese, until smooth. Add the sifted powdered sugar, milk, vanilla extract and salt. Mix on low until well combined. If the icing is too runny, add an additional ¼ cup of powdered sugar at a time, until desired consistency. Icing should be spreadable and not too thick. Slather maple cream cheese icing before serving. Enjoy!

